# Frontend Standards

## Templ Templates

- **File Extension**: Use `.templ` extension for all templates
- **Generated Files**: Auto-generated `*_templ.go` files from `.templ` files
- **Build Process**: Include `templ generate` in build pipeline
- **Method Components**: Use method components for better organization
- **Type Safety**: Leverage compile-time type checking

### Template Structure

```go
// views/example.templ
templ ExampleComponent(data Data) {
    <div class="container">
        <h1>{ data.Title }</h1>
    </div>
}
```

## HTMX Integration

- **Library Inclusion**: HTMX library included in HTML templates
- **Dynamic Interactions**: Use HTMX attributes (hx-get, hx-post, hx-target, etc.)
- **Credentials**: Configure HTMX to send cookies and credentials
- **Endpoints**: Backend provides HTMX-compatible endpoints for voting and admin operations

### HTMX Patterns

```html
<button hx-post="/vote" hx-target="#results" hx-swap="innerHTML">
    Vote
</button>
```

## Tailwind CSS

- **Configuration**: `tailwind.config.js` with custom theme configuration
- **Custom Colors**: Use custom color palette (goat, tavern themes)
- **Utility Classes**: Use Tailwind utility classes for styling
- **Build Process**: CSS built from `input.css` to compiled `style.css`

### Custom Theme Colors

```javascript
colors: {
  'goat': {
    300: '#a0a0a0',
    400: '#9ca3af',
    500: '#404040',
    // ...
  },
  'tavern': {
    300: '#f0d75a',
    400: '#e6c547',
    // ...
  }
}
```

## Responsive Design

- **Mobile-first**: Design for mobile devices first
- **Breakpoints**: Use Tailwind responsive prefixes (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)
- **Touch-friendly**: Ensure buttons and interactive elements are touch-friendly

## Performance

- **Static Assets**: Optimize images and assets
- **CSS Purging**: Use Tailwind's purge functionality
- **HTMX Efficiency**: Minimize DOM updates and server requests
